.env
node_modules/
out/
data/*

# known-bad.json is a small PUBLIC seed the decentralized screen needs at runtime — track it (the rest of data/ stays ignored: generated/large artifacts)
!data/known-bad.json
# issuer-verified.json is the small, curated, ISSUER-OFFICIAL registry (on-chain-verified addresses) — ships so /asset can show the green "issuer-verified" without the non-commercial Coingecko file.
!data/issuer-verified.json
# token-radar's memory: every token it ever judged, the call it made at first sight, and how that token
# actually ended up. This is the one asset that cannot be copied by reading the code — it only accrues by
# watching the market over time, and the misses are recorded alongside the hits on purpose. Versioned so the
# track record is auditable by whoever doubts it. (observations.jsonl stays local: append-only, re-derivable.)
!data/token-radar/
!data/token-radar/tokens.json
!data/token-radar/scorecard.json
data/token-radar/observations.jsonl
dist/

# Hermes agent cron output (generated per-run)
hermes/agents/*/cache/

# x402 anti-replay runtime store (not source)
data/x402-consumed.json
